+// motion is "consistent" when the current frame shows content with that
+// motion at its current endpoint (it is its own fixed point).
+//  - A consistent and both endpoints agree: the midpoint stands (A first,
+//    so wherever the old path was right this changes nothing).
+//  - else B consistent and agreeing: the object whose path crosses this
+//    pixel at this instant though the flow here belongs to what is behind.
+//  - else revealed (the previous endpoint is confirmed taken by the other
+//    motion): the current frame's sample alone; covered (the current
+//    endpoint is confirmed taken by the other motion): the previous frame's.
+//  - else the old composition.
+// All of it as weights, faded in by how clearly there are two motions and
+// how strongly the frames disagree, so nothing switches hard from frame to
+// frame. With the bidirectional flow its cycle check is part of flow_trust.
+float4 occlusion_aware_midpoint(
+    float2 pixel,
+    float2 backward,
+    CameraSample previous_a,
+    CameraSample current_a,
+    float disagreement_a,
+    float flow_trust,
